  "worked_solution": "Let $L,$ $W,$ $H$ and $V$ be the length, the width, the height, and the volume of the box, respectively. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L=12\\text{\u00a0cm},\\, & W=5\\text{\u00a0cm}, \\\\ H=4\\text{\u00a0cm},\\, & \\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-0.2\\text{\u00a0cm/s}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-0.1\\text{\u00a0cm/s},\\, & \\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-0.05\\text{\u00a0cm/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the four variables is given by the formula for the volume of a rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=LWH\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides of $V=LWH$ with respect to $t,$ using the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}V & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWH) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =W\\cdot H(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t})+L\\cdot H(\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t})+L\\cdot W(\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(5)(4)(-0.2)+(12)(4)(-0.1)+(12)(5)(-0.05) \\\\  & =-11.8{\\text{\u00a0cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the bar of soap is decreasing at a rate of $11.8{\\text{\u00a0cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}.$",
